    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Caryota urens」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caryota_urens",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1377460759,
      "text": "Caryota urens is a species of flowering plant in the palm family, native to Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Malaysia and India, where they grow in fields and rainforest clearings, it is regarded as introduced in Cambodia. The epithet urens is Latin for \"stinging\" alluding to the chemicals in the fruit. Common names in English include solitary fishtail palm, kithul palm, toddy palm, wine palm, sago palm and jaggery palm. Its leaf is used as fishing rod after trimming the branches of the leaf and drying. According to Monier-Williams, it is called moha-karin in Sanskrit. It is one of the sugar palms."
    }
  },
